#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:1
msgid "Contributing Basics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:3
msgid "An overview on contributing to the _Black_ project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:5
msgid ""
"If you are making a large change, please open an issue first to discuss it "
"beforehand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:7
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:9
msgid ""
"Development on the latest version of Python is preferred. You can use any "
"operating system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:12
msgid "First clone the _Black_ repository:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:14
msgid ""
"$ git clone https://github.com/psf/black.git\n"
"$ cd black\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:19
msgid ""
"Then install development dependencies inside a virtual environment of your "
"choice, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:22
msgid ""
"$ python3 -m venv .venv\n"
"$ source .venv/bin/activate # activation for linux and mac\n"
"$ .venv\\Scripts\\activate # activation for windows\n"
"\n"
"(.venv)$ pip install --group dev\n"
"(.venv)$ pip install -e \".[d]\"\n"
"(.venv)$ pre-commit install\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:32
msgid ""
"Before submitting pull requests, run lints and tests with the following "
"commands from the root of the black repo:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:35
msgid ""
"(.venv)$ tox -e run_self # Format Black itself (required!)\n"
"(.venv)$ pre-commit run -a # Linting\n"
"(.venv)$ tox -e py # Unit tests (also run by CI)\n"
"(.venv)$ tox -e fuzz # Fuzz testing (optional)\n"
"\n"
"(.venv)$ tox --parallel=auto # Run format, tests, and fuzz in parallel\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:44
msgid "News / Changelog Requirement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:46
msgid ""
"`Black` has CI that will check for an entry corresponding to your PR in "
"`CHANGES.md`. If you feel your PR does not require a changelog entry, please "
"state that and a maintainer can add the `ci: skip news` label to bypass the "
"check. Otherwise, please ensure you have a line in the following format "
"added below the appropriate header:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:51
msgid "- `Black` is now more awesome (#X)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:55
msgid ""
"Note that X should be your PR number, not issue number! To workout X, you "
"may use [Next PR Number](https://ichard26.github.io/next-pr-number/?"
"owner=psf&name=black)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:58
msgid ""
"The description should be no more than two sentences and should accurately "
"describe the user-facing change. Avoid referencing Black internals or the "
"implementation details of the change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:62
msgid ""
"This saves a lot of release overhead as the releaser does not need to work "
"out what to add to the `CHANGES.md` for each commit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:65
msgid "Style Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:67
msgid ""
"If a change would affect the advertised code style, please modify [the "
"documentation](https://black.readthedocs.io/en/latest/the_black_code_style/"
"current_style.html) to reflect that change. Patches that fix unintended bugs "
"in formatting don't need to be mentioned separately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:72
msgid ""
"Please familiarize yourself with our [stability policy](labels/stability-"
"policy). Most style changes must be added to the `--preview` style. "
"Exceptions are fixing crashes or changes that would not affect an already-"
"formatted file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:76
msgid ""
"New formatting styles are implemented by adding a new item to the `Preview` "
"enum in `mode.py`. The name of this style should accurately summarize the "
"user-facing change in about 3-6 words and under 40 characters. All new "
"formatting logic should be gated under a `Preview.FEATURE in mode` check. "
"[The diff-shades check](https://black.readthedocs.io/en/latest/contributing/"
"gauging_changes.html#diff-shades) ensures this is implemented correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:83
msgid ""
"If the change is implemented under the `--preview` or `--unstable` style, "
"please include the change in the [Future Style document](https://black."
"readthedocs.io/en/latest/the_black_code_style/future_style.html) instead. "
"Additionally, please ensure you include the changelog entry under the "
"dedicated \"Preview style\" heading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:89
msgid "Testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:91
msgid ""
"All aspects of the _Black_ style should be tested. PRs are welcome to add "
"tests for parts of Black that aren't covered by existing tests. "
"Additionally, if you come across a resolved but unclosed issue, please PR "
"test cases for it before we close it, if they don't exist already."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:96
msgid ""
"It's a good practice to follow Test-Driven Development: If you're fixing a "
"bug, first add a test. Run it to confirm it fails, then fix the bug, and run "
"the test again to confirm it's really fixed. Please add tests for any and "
"all changes you make."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:100
msgid ""
"Whenever possible, tests should be created as files in the `tests/data/"
"cases` directory. These files consist of up to three parts:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:103
msgid ""
"A line that starts with `# flags: ` followed by a set of command-line "
"options. For example, if the line is `# flags: --preview --skip-magic-"
"trailing-comma`, the test case will be run with preview mode on and the "
"magic trailing comma off. The options accepted are mostly a subset of those "
"of _Black_ itself, except for the `--minimum-version=` flag, which should be "
"used when testing a grammar feature that works only in newer versions of "
"Python. This flag ensures that we don't try to validate the AST on older "
"versions and tests that we autodetect the Python version correctly when the "
"feature is used. For the exact flags accepted, see the function "
"`get_flags_parser` in `tests/util.py`. If this line is omitted, the default "
"options are used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:113
msgid "A block of Python code used as input for the formatter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:114
msgid ""
"The line `# output`, followed by the output of _Black_ when run on the "
"previous block. If this is omitted, the test asserts that _Black_ will leave "
"the input code unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:117
msgid "Test Arguments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:119
msgid "Run tests on a specific python version:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:121
msgid "(.venv)$ tox -e py314\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:125
msgid "Run an individual test:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:127
msgid "(.venv)$ pytest -k <test name>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:131
msgid "Pass arguments to pytest:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:133
msgid "(.venv)$ tox -e py -- --no-cov\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:137
msgid ""
"_Black_ also has two unique CLI options that serve to help depug failing "
"test files in `tests/data/`. These can be passed to `pytest` through `tox` "
"as shown above, or directly into pytest if not using `tox`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:141
msgid ""
"`--print-full-tree` prints the full concrete syntax tree (CST) upon a "
"failing test. Both the CST after parsing the input (\"actual\") and the CST "
"after parsing the output (\"expected\") are printed. Note that a test can "
"fail with different formatting outputs but the same CST."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:146
msgid "(.venv)$ tox -e py -- --print-full-tree\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:150
msgid ""
"`--print-tree-diff` prints the diff of the two CSTs described above upon a "
"failing test. This is the default. To turn it off pass `--print-tree-"
"diff=False`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:153
msgid "(.venv)$ tox -e py -- --print-tree-diff=False\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:157
msgid "Docs Testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:159
msgid "If you make changes to docs, you can test they still build locally:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:161
msgid ""
"(.venv)$ pip install --group docs\n"
"(.venv)$ pip install -e \".[d]\"\n"
"(.venv)$ sphinx-build -a -b html -W docs/ docs/_build/\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:167
msgid "Thank You!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing/the_basics.md:169
msgid ""
"Thanks again for your interest in improving the project! You're taking "
"action when most people decide to sit and watch."
msgstr ""
